From fc31ecc13acd425abe5a8e3aaec76b1c25abc8b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CharlyRien <9572419+CharlyRien@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 17:57:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 27/29] Lab: XCL_RT_WATCH=N (off) logs named structures'
 headers, CPU against video memory, and the builder's dispatches

Every N frames (at least 30), once a ray-tracing structure view or a watched pipeline was seen:
- each structure a view names in unified memory: header words 0, 1, 3, 12 (root, @0x30) and 13
  as the CPU sees them and as video memory holds them (sparse::peek_gpu: a copy into a vector of
  its own, the CPU's view untouched), bytes with video memory, bytes that differ, and the watched
  records whose dispatches were given an address in that header;
- XCL_RT_WATCH_WRITERS (record hashes): 16 bytes at each root address their dispatches got;
- XCL_RT_WATCH_RECORDS (file of record hashes): pipelines, dispatches launched / put off / without
  a translated pipeline / failed, dropped put-offs, DispatchX calls without flag 0x8000, largest x.
Nothing changes with the switch unset. Not in TRANSLATOR_SOURCES.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
